        <body>
            
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="tam-Latn" rendition="class:tamil maturity:vernacular">
                
                <ab>		
                    <lb n="1"/><hi rend="grantha">svasti śrī</hi>
                </ab>
                
                <p>
                    <hi rend="grantha">śrī</hi>-kaṉṉāra-tēvarkku yā
                    <lb n="2" break="no"/>ṇṭu patt’ oṉpat-āvatu
                </p>
                <p>
                    vākūr <hi rend="grantha">śrī</hi>-m<choice><orig>u</orig><reg>ū</reg></choice>la<hi rend="grantha">stā</hi>
                    <lb n="3" break="no"/>ṉattu <hi rend="grantha">mahāde</hi>varkku Iṟai-p-puṇai-c-cēriyu
                    <lb n="4" break="no"/>ṭaiyāṉ vāṭṭuḻati nānūṟṟuva<choice><orig>n</orig><reg>ṉ</reg></choice>-ākiya mummu
                    <lb n="5" break="no"/>ṭi-c-cōḻa-p-pallavaraiyaṉ ca<choice><orig>ṉ</orig><reg>n</reg></choice>tirātitta
                    <lb n="6" break="no"/>val vaytta na<choice><orig>ṉ</orig><reg>n</reg></choice>tā-vilakk’ oṉṟiṉukku <hi rend="grantha">vai</hi>t
                    <lb n="7" break="no"/>ta cāvā m<choice><orig>u</orig><reg>ū</reg></choice>vā pēr-āṭu toṇṇūṟu
                </p>
                <p>
                    Ivai
                   <lb n="8"/><hi rend="grantha"> panmāheśvarar·</hi> I<hi rend="grantha">rakṣai</hi>
                </p>
                    
                   
            </div>
            
            <div type="apparatus">
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1">Hail! Prosperity!</p>
                <p n="1-2">Year nineteen <supplied reason="subaudible">of the reign</supplied> of śrī-Kaṉṉara-tēvar.</p> 
                <p n="2-7">The never dying and never ageing sheep donated by Vāṭṭuḻati Nāṉūṟṟuvaṉ alias Mummuṭi-c-cōḻa-p-pallavaraiyaṉ of Iṟaippuṇai-c-cēri for a perpetual lamp to the great Lord of śrī-Mūlastāṉam of Vākūr, as long as the moon and the sun will last, are ninety.</p> 
                <p n="7-8">These are under the protection of the great Śaiva devotees <supplied reason="explanation">Māheśvaras</supplied>.</p>
            </div>
            
